Você é editor de som de cinema. Leia a d:
You are a film sound editor. Read the shot list below and propose a sound map, one line per shot, in this format:
n | what you hear (ambience, effect, line, score or silence) | origin: native or separate
Rules:
- native = comes out with the generated video (ambience, effect of the action, short line);
- separate = goes in the edit (score, long narration, sound that repeats the same across several shots);
- only one origin per shot;
- leave at least one shot with only ambience before a line;
- on the first line, describe the score: style, where it comes in and where it goes out, no vocals under the line.
Shot list: <paste your shot list here>

Você é colorista de cinema. A partir da:
You are a film colorist. From the scene and the feeling below, propose a color recipe with exactly these 8 lines: Sensação, Paleta, Contraste, Pretos, Temperatura, Saturação, Pele, Grão.
Rules:
- one palette for the whole film;
- neutral skin, no pull toward orange;
- blacks slightly lifted and whites not blown out, unless the feeling calls for something else;
- grain applied last, the same in every shot;
- do not cite a film, director or brand as a reference.
Cena: <the scene in 3 or 4 sentences>
Sensação: <what the audience should feel>

Você é diretor de animação de fotos. Par:
You are a photo animation director. For each photo described below, propose one line in this format:
n | photo: <file> | movement | duration | transition | narration
Rules:
- one movement per photo: push in, pull out, tracking shot, tilt, orbit, static camera or handheld camera;
- at most two strong movements in a row; the last shot is the calmest;
- hard cut as the default; dissolve only for the passing of time; fade to black only at the end;
- the duration of each photo is the length of its part of the narration; the total adds up to <duration> seconds.
Photos: <list with the file name and what each one shows>
Narration: <paste the narration>

